          "answer": "No, your loved one's primary home is exempt from the $5,000 individual or $6,000 couple asset limits. One vehicle is also exempt. The limits apply mainly to bank accounts, investments, and cash. If your loved one has significant non-exempt assets, ask the ADRC about spend-down options."
