      "intro": "If you are caring for an aging parent or a family member with a disability, Texas Respite Care Services can send a trained worker to your parent's home so you can step away for hours, a day, or longer without arranging and paying for care yourself. Depending on the program your family qualifies for, that relief can be planned in advance or arranged on short notice in an emergency.\n\nTexas does not run respite care as a single program. Instead, three different funding streams can pay for it: the STAR+PLUS Medicaid waiver (up to 30 days of respite per year for eligible waiver members), the Texas Lifespan Respite Care Program (brief in-home or out-of-home relief for caregivers of people with chronic conditions or disabilities of any age), and local Area Agency on Aging voucher programs (funds to help adult caregivers of people 60 or older who need help with at least two daily activities, or for grandparents 55 and older raising a child or person with a disability). Which stream your family accesses depends on your parent's situation, not on a single statewide income threshold.\n\nBecause access and wait times depend heavily on your county, the fastest first step is calling the Aging and Disability Resource Center at 1-855-YES-ADRC (1-855-937-2372). They screen for all three funding streams and connect you to the right local program.",
